- provider-neutral descriptors, no Apollo/Clay/Apify/etc. lock-in;
- local/public/licensed evidence can compete on evidence tier, quality, measured success, cost and latency;
- unconfigured external providers are blocked rather than silently planned;
- terms/allowed-purpose must be confirmed for external API providers;
- a paid provider without pricing source + verification date is blocked, so projected cost cannot be fabricated;
- already-sufficient fresh/non-conflicting evidence skips provider work;
- stale or conflicting existing evidence does not suppress refresh;
- external providers per field are hard capped;
- work-email stop rule explicitly rejects inferred private addresses;
- projected cost remains a projection: `providerCalls=0`, `externalEffects=0`, `businessEffectAuthority=NONE`, `executionStatus=NOT_RUN`.

