Systems Integration independently reproduced the architectural cause on canonical BLACK SKY main `2ce97af4bafa05db3dbeec3a83320186ea06a956`: `runAgentMeshCycle()` performs `getAgentMeshCycleReceipt()` and returns immediately for `existing.state === 'STARTED'`; `reconcileAbandonedAgentMeshCycles()` sits later on the new-occurrence path. Therefore same-occurrence redelivery after a crash can remain wedged indefinitely if the scheduler keeps delivering the same occurrence.

Current canonical repro is PR #139, deliberately non-colliding with active #134/#135/#131. Integration acceptance is slightly stronger than the initial issue text:

- preserve identity validation before any abandoned-cycle terminalization;
- `age < abandonedCycleAfterMs` stays STARTED/BLOCKED with zero replay;
- explicitly define and test the equality boundary `age === abandonedCycleAfterMs`;
- `age >/= threshold` (whichever policy is chosen) terminalizes that exact STARTED cycle as DEGRADED / `cycle-abandoned-before-terminal`, with null/empty firstSweep/workers/secondSweep and zero work/provider replay;
- two concurrent recoverers must converge to exactly one durable terminal receipt and semantically identical observed terminal truth;
- repeated post-terminal delivery remains idempotent;
- real PostgreSQL concurrency proof is required, not only the JSON/in-memory serialized path.

Do not solve this by globally reconciling abandoned cycles before identity lookup in a way that allows the same occurrence to fall through into a new cycle. Exact-occurrence recovery should return the terminalized receipt immediately. No external effects.

